:name: CFU-Playground - TFLM with a Verilated hardware accelerator
:description: Real TensorFlow Lite Micro on VexRiscv with a co-simulated Custom Function Unit.

# This wraps Renode's BUILT-IN CFU-Playground demo. It runs real TFLM
# software on a LiteX/VexRiscv SoC whose CPU has a Custom Function Unit
# (CFU) -- extra "silicon" that accelerates the int8 multiply-accumulate
# at the heart of quantized inference. Renode CO-SIMULATES that CFU with
# Verilator (the .cs peripheral drives a Verilated C++ model).
#
# IMPORTANT / caveats (unlike labs 00-10, this one is NOT self-contained):
#   * First run DOWNLOADS a prebuilt Verilated binary + TFLM software
#     from dl.antmicro.com -> needs internet.
#   * The Verilated binary is compiled for x86-64 Linux, so this works in
#     a standard (x86-64) Codespace but NOT on arm64 hosts.
#
# The bundled script lives inside the Renode install; `@scripts/...`
# resolves against Renode's root. It creates the machine, wires the CFU,
# downloads the assets, and loads the software. We just start it.

i @scripts/single-node/litex_vexriscv_verilated_cfu.resc

#start

echo ""
echo "In the UART analyzer, use the interactive menu:"
echo "  (2) Functional CFU Test   - exercise the accelerator"
echo "  (1) TfLM Models menu      - run a model with the CFU"
echo "Compare cycle counts with/without the CFU to see the speedup."
